From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 12:32:12 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 11061/11362] Fail at commit time when an eval-run consumer
 reads a field nothing emits (REQ-ARC-WMTE-6642/6643)

Three consumers in three days ran against eval-run fields no artifact
recorded (trajectory_supervisor, generator_channels, the
induction_attempts round provenance exp6968 blocks on), each found only
after the GPU-hours were spent. Three changes close the class:

1. scripts/eval_run_consumer_field_lint.py: every tracked .py naming
   results/arc_leaderboard_eval_runs must declare EVAL_RUN_FIELDS_READ,
   and every declared field must exist in a real artifact or in producer
   source. Fails closed with no artifacts; always prints populations so
   zero findings is distinguishable from never-looked. Wired as the
   eval-run-consumer-field-lint pre-commit hook and registered in
   GUARD_TARGETS (the sealed-file edit is declared under scope id
   eval-run-field-join-20260904). Declarations seeded in all 6 existing
   consumers. Born-firing check: it flagged exactly the three unemitted
   provenance fields before change 2 wired them.

2. REQ-ARC-WMTE-6643: round rows now carry engine_emitted_at and
   prompt_sha256 (from the attempt archiver, which now returns
   ts/sha256_full/prompt_sha256), and induce rounds persist a
   transition-source file (rows, shown/held-out split, engine-binding
   hash) whose path lands on the row. This is what exp6968 needs to
   resolve an engine without the manifest fallback that breaks on the
   first deduplicated re-emission. Refactor rounds stay unrecorded --
   their feedback rows have no stable identity yet; stated in the spec.

3. exp6968's early-return sentinel no longer reports a hardcoded-False
   immutable_transition_source: it names the upstream gates that
   actually failed (same class as REQ-CONDUCTOR-VERDICT-3).

Mutation-proven, all three: lint neither-place branch softened -> RED,
restored byte-identically -> GREEN; row wiring dropped -> RED, induce
branch disabled -> RED, restored -> GREEN; sentinel reverted -> RED,
restored -> GREEN. 30 tests pass across the three touched suites.

